<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John of Saxony</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1801–1873</span> · Also known as King John of Saxony</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> was king of Saxony from 1854 to 1873. A scholar as well as a monarch, he translated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dante-alighieri">Dante</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/divine-comedy">Divine Comedy</a> into German under the pen name Philalethes. He sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-prussian-war">Austro-Prussian War</a> of 1866, after which Saxony had to join the Prussian-led North German Confederation and, in 1871, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a>.</p></div>
